/E (in drone engineering regarding processing power versus flight endurance. Embedded microcontrollers, such as the ESP32, are excellent for timing-sensitive tasks like Pulse Width Modulation \(PWM\) generation, but their RISC architecture is incapable of executing the billions of floating-point operations required by modern convolutional neural networks \(CNNs\). Conversely, integrating a heavy onboard GPU \(such as an NVIDIA Jetson )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
