/E (The system study for AeroEye explores the architectural requirements and hardware-software synchronization necessary for an autonomous quadcopter. It adopts a "distributed brain" model, decoupling high-level cognitive tasks like YOLOv8 inference from low-level stabilization. By utilizing a tri-node ecosystem \(Smartphone, GCS, and ESP32\), the study establishes a method to overcome the computational and weight limitations of hobbyist-grade UAVs. )
/Pg 17 0 R
