/E (The most critical flaw in manual systems is the human physiological limit. The average human reaction time is approximately 250ms. In high-speed tracking, where a target might change direction in under 100ms, the pilot is perpetually reactive. This delay results in "Pilot-Induced Oscillation" \(PIO\), where over-correction leads to an unstable flight path. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
746 0 obj
<<
