/S /P
/P 578 0 R
/E (Existing autonomous drones typically rely on Global Positioning System \(GPS\) waypoints. These systems are "coordinate-aware" rather than "object-aware." They use a magnetometer and GPS module to move between pre-defined longitudinal and latitudinal points. While effective for high-altitude mapping, they possess no inherent ability to "see" or identify specific subjects, such as a person or a vehicle, without additional, highly expensive specialized hardware. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
