789 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 581 0 R
/E (By offloading the heavy AI processing to a Ground Control Station, the proposed system achieves a significantly higher Power-to-Weight Ratio. Traditional autonomous drones require expensive and heavy onboard computers \(like a Jetson Nano\), which drain the 3S LiPo battery rapidly. Our system uses a lightweight smartphone and an ESP32, allowing the drone to remain agile and extend its flight time while still benefiting from the processing power of a high-end laptop GPU. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
790 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 581 0 R
/E (Unlike existing systems that are "blind" to the objects they navigate around, the proposed system possesses true semantic awareness. By utilizing the YOLOv8 architecture, the drone can distinguish between different classes of objects. This means the drone isn't just following a "blob" of color; it is identifying a specific human or vehicle. This allows for a much higher level of reliability in complex environments where background clutter would normally cause a standard autonomous drone to lose its lock. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
791 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 581 0 R
/E (The AeroEye architecture offers several transformative advantages over existing manual and GPS- based drone systems, specifically in the areas of computational efficiency, operational precision, and safety. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
