817 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 583 0 R
/E (Hardware Synchronization: The ESP32-WROOM provides a dual-core architecture that is uniquely suited for autonomous flight. Unlike single-core microcontrollers that may experience "interrupt latency" while waiting for a network packet, the ESP32 can simultaneously manage the high-speed UDP socket and the precise 50Hz PWM signals required by the 2200KV brushless motors. This allows the drone to process motor-mixing math on one core while the other core remains "on guard" for incoming AI commands, ensuring zero-jitter performance. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
818 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 583 0 R
/E (Algorithmic Efficiency and Inference: The selection of the YOLOv8 \(You Only Look Once\) architecture is a critical technical decision. It provides the optimal balance between mean Average Precision \(mAP\) and inference speed. By offloading this task to a Ground Control Station \(GCS\) equipped with a dedicated GPU, the system maintains a frame rate of 30+ FPS. This high-frequency visual update is essential for calculating the real-time spatial errors required by the PID control loops. Without this offloading, an onboard processor would suffer from "thermal throttling," leading to dropped frames and inevitable flight instability. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
