/P 585 0 R
/E (GPS-Denied Operational Capability: Because the system relies on local computer vision rather than satellite triangulation, it is operationally feasible in "GPS-denied" environments. This includes indoor warehouses, dense forest canopies, or urban "canyons" where GPS signals are often jammed or reflected. This makes AeroEye more versatile than standard commercial drones that require a "Home Point" lock before take- off. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
837 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 585 0 R
/E (Intuitive Telemetry Monitoring: The CustomTkinter-based GUI provides the operator with a "cockpit" view of the autonomous process. Real-time feedback, such as the "FC: CONNECTED" status and the Current Estimation \(Amps\), allows the user to monitor the health of the 3S LiPo battery and the thermal status of the 2200KV motors. This transparency ensures that the operator can intervene manually if environmental conditions exceed the drone's operational limits. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
838 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 585 0 R
/E (Software Watchdog and Fail-Safe Logic: Safety is the primary operational concern for autonomous drones. The project implements a 500ms heartbeat window. If the ESP32 does not receive a valid UDP packet within this timeframe, the "Software Watchdog" automatically overrides the GCS commands and initiates a Controlled Landing Mode. This prevents the "Fly-Away" scenarios common in DIY drones and ensures that the drone descends safely even during a total Wi-Fi blackout. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
