/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 586 0 R
/E (System Analysis represents the analytical cornerstone of the AeroEye project. This phase is dedicated to deconstructing the complex interplay between autonomous computer vision and physical flight dynamics. The objective of this analysis is to transform the broad goals of the project into a set of precise technical requirements and modular definitions. By treating the drone not as a standalone toy, but as a Distributed Cyber-Physical System \(DCPS\), we can analyze the continuous data flow from the moment a photon hits the smartphone camera sensor to the millisecond a PWM signal alters the RPM of a brushless motor. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
847 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 586 0 R
/E (The analysis focuses on the "Inference-to-Action" pipeline. In high-speed robotics, the bottleneck is rarely the hardware's top speed, but rather the system's ability to process information and make decisions. Our analysis identifies that the most efficient way to achieve real-time tracking is through Computational Offloading. By separating the system into logical layers Perception, Decision, and Execution we ensure that each component operates at its maximum efficiency. This modularity also ensures system resilience; if one software component fails or requires an update, the underlying flight stabilization remains intact, preventing catastrophic hardware loss. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
