/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 588 0 R
/E (Residing on the ESP32-WROOM microcontroller, this module acts as the "Muscles." It operates on a dual-core architecture to ensure zero-latency execution. Core 1 is dedicated to the UDP Telemetry Listener, which parses incoming command strings from the GCS and converts them into stabilized motor values. Core 0 is dedicated to the Software Watchdog and Motor Mixing. It generates 16-bit high-resolution PWM signals for the four Electronic Speed Controllers \(ESCs\). Most importantly, this module handles the "Failsafe Protocol." It constantly monitors the "Heartbeat" of the GCS; if no data is received for 500ms, it overrides all autonomous commands and initiates a gradual, controlled descent to the ground. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
877 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
