/P 595 0 R
/E (\(EMI\) that can corrupt the 50Hz PWM signals. Furthermore, the smartphone mount is designed with a mechanical vibration dampening system. Because the YOLOv8 model relies on sharp edge detection for bounding box accuracy, any high-frequency vibration from the 2200KV motors could cause 'motion blur,' leading to a tracking failure. This section also considers the aerodynamic impact of the smartphone's surface area; the PID controller is tuned to compensate for the increased wind resistance caused by the phone, ensuring that the drone's tilt during forward flight does not result in a loss of altitude. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [9]
>>
