/E (The Unified Modeling Language \(UML\) serves as the standard graphical language for visualizing, specifying, constructing, and documenting the artifacts of a software-intensive system. In the context of the AeroEye project, UML is not merely a documentation tool but a critical engineering blueprint that bridges the gap between high-level AI logic and low-level hardware execution. Given the distributed nature of this system where data must flow seamlessly across a network of three distinct devices UML provides the necessary clarity to ensure that object-oriented principles are maintained across the Python and C++ environments. )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
990 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 596 0 R
/E (By utilizing UML, we can model the complex, time-sensitive interactions of the "Perception- Action" loop. It allows us to define how the YOLOv8 detection classes interact with the PID control classes, and how the ESP32 handles concurrent tasks like network listening and motor- mixing. This formal modeling ensures that the system is scalable, modular, and robust against logic errors that could lead to catastrophic hardware failure during flight. )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [7]
>>
