/T (Mechanical Actuation \(PWM\): On the hardware side, the output design focuses on the generation of Pulse Width Modulation \(PWM\) signals. The ESP32 translates received digital strings into high-resolution electrical pulses. These pulses dictate the RPM of the brushless motors, effectively turning mathematical PID logic into aerial maneuverability. )
/E (Mechanical Actuation \(PWM\): On the hardware side, the output design focuses on the generation of Pulse Width Modulation \(PWM\) signals. The ESP32 translates received digital strings into high-resolution electrical pulses. These pulses dictate the RPM of the brushless motors, effectively turning mathematical PID logic into aerial maneuverability. )
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [3]
>>
