/P 611 0 R
/E (The source code for the AeroEye system is a hybrid implementation designed to bridge the gap between high-level machine perception and low-level hardware actuation. The software architecture is split into two primary components: a Python-based Ground Control Station and a C++ based firmware for the ESP32 microcontroller. The Python code handles the computationally intensive tasks of YOLOv8 object detection and PID error derivation, while the C++ firmware manages the real-time constraints of PWM signal generation and failsafe monitoring. The following code segments document the logic used to establish the UDP handshake, the coordinate mapping system, and the motor-mixing algorithms required for autonomous flight. )
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
