1830 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 653 0 R
/E (A primary focus was placed on minimizing latency in the UDP Communication Link between the Python-based GCS and the ESP32 microcontroller. Unlike TCP, the UDP protocol was selected for its low overhead, but it requires a robust parsing logic to handle potential packet loss. We conducted "Packet Throughput Tests" to ensure the firmware could accurately parse 8-bit command strings while simultaneously maintaining the Current Limiting Logic required to protect the ESCs under high-torque loads. By monitoring the Serial output of the ESP32 during high-speed maneuvers, we verified that the dual-core architecture successfully isolated the Wi-Fi stack from the PWM generation, ensuring that a spike in network traffic never caused a motor "stutter." )
/Pg 93 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
