1922 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 662 0 R
/E (The operational workflow of the AeroEye system is governed by a rigorous pre-flight initialization sequence designed to ensure the absolute integrity of both the computer vision engine and the physical flight hardware. Operation commences with the activation of the Ground Control Station \(GCS\) and the establishment of a dedicated 2.4GHz Wi-Fi access point, optimized for low-latency UDP traffic. Once the ESP32 microcontroller is energized via the 3S LiPo battery, it performs an automated self-diagnostic check indicated by a rapid LED status pattern to verify the health of the onboard sensors and the Wi-Fi stack. The operator must confirm a "Handshake Successful" status on the GCS interface before the system attempts to authenticate with the network. )
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1923 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 662 0 R
/E (A critical phase of the operation is the SimonK Arming Sequence. To prevent accidental motor spin-up, the drone must remain perfectly stationary for a minimum of two seconds while the ESCs receive a synchronized 1000-microsecond "Zero-Throttle" pulse. This unlocks the propulsion system and readies the motors for high-frequency PWM adjustments. Following the "ESCs Armed" notification, the operator initializes the Python-based vision script, which loads the YOLOv8 neural network weights into the GCS system memory. The live MJPEG video feed is then monitored for "Detection Confidence." If the neural network identifies the target with a confidence score above 0.5, the lighting conditions are deemed sufficient, and the system is cleared for its primary mission. )
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1924 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 662 0 R
/E (During active operation, the system functions in a semi-autonomous state, often referred to as "Human-in-the-Loop" \(HITL\) control. The pilot manages the initial vertical ascent to a safe hover altitude typically 1.7 meters using manual throttle overrides to ensure the drone clears any immediate ground-level obstacles. Once a person is detected in the video frame, the operator uses the GCS interface to click on the target's bounding box, transitioning the craft into "Locked Tracking Mode." At this stage, the operation is governed by the Triple-Axis PID control loop, which autonomously manages pitch, roll, and yaw to maintain center-frame alignment and a constant 2.0-meter safety distance. )
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
