<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 663 0 R
/E (From an electrical perspective, the 3S Lithium-Polymer \(LiPo\) battery requires the most stringent maintenance protocols. To avoid permanent chemical degradation and the risk of "cell swelling," the battery must never be discharged below a critical threshold of 3.2V per cell. Following every flight session, the batteries must be transitioned to a "Storage Voltage" of approximately 3.8V per cell using a balanced charger. Additionally, the motor-to-ESC bullet connectors and the XT60 power interface should be inspected for signs of carbonization or heat-induced discoloration. Such signs indicate excessive resistance and suggest that the "Current Limiting" threshold in the C++ firmware should be recalibrated to a lower value to prevent electrical fire or component burnout. Software maintenance is equally vital, as the "Digital Health" of the system directly impacts flight stability. The YOLOv8 model weights should be periodically re-evaluated and fine-tuned if the )
/Pg 103 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
