1932 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 663 0 R
/E (The operator's role shifts to "Systems Monitor," remaining vigilant of the real-time telemetry displayed on the Head-Up Display \(HUD\). This includes monitoring the estimated current draw \(not to exceed the 25A safety limit\) and observing the Packet Acknowledgment \(ACK\) signals. If the UDP latency spikes above 100 milliseconds due to external signal interference, the operator is trained to intervene manually, bringing the craft to a lower, stable hover to prevent hardware strain. The operation concludes with a manual descent or by triggering the software "Disarm" command via the GCS, which immediately cuts power to the brushless motors once the craft has achieved a safe landing. )
/Pg 103 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
