2019 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 670 0 R
/E (Beyond simple documentation, this section includes a precise breakdown of the ESP32-WROOM- 32 GPIO pin-mapping, providing a clear roadmap of how the flight controller translates digital commands into 16-bit PWM signals across the F450 frame. This documentation is supplemented by a serialized log of the UDP telemetry packets exchanged between the Ground Control Station and the drone, illustrating the exact Pitch, Roll, and Yaw values required to maintain a stable 2.0- meter tracking distance. Furthermore, the appendix catalogs the specific calibration constants and weights used in the YOLOv8 inference engine, alongside the coordinate transform matrices that allow the Python control script to convert pixel-based bounding boxes into real-world physical maneuvers. )
/Pg 110 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
2020 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 670 0 R
/E (The appendix serves as an exhaustive repository of supplementary technical data, multi- dimensional visualizations, and granular code documentation designed to provide a comprehensive deep-dive into the AeroEye project's structural management and distributed technical architecture. These materials function as the vital empirical backbone of the primary report, offering a detailed analysis of the rigorous scheduling parameters, complex electronic interfacing, and the underlying mathematical logic utilized to stabilize the quadcopter during high- latency autonomous tracking sessions. By documenting the "low-level" configurations that govern the interaction between the software and hardware layers, this section ensures that every aspect of the project is transparent, verifiable, and prepared for future academic or commercial reproduction. )
/Pg 110 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
