4263 0 obj
<<
/Title (AeroEye is specifically engineered to overcome these four hurdles by utilizing a multi-threaded Python Ground Control Station \(GCS\), an ultra-fast UDP telemetry stream, and a dual-core ESP32 firmware architecture that segregates communication tasks from motor actuation. By solving these gaps, the project aims to demonstrate that professional-grade autonomy can be achieved through optimized software-hardware synergy rather than expensive, heavy onboard hardware.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 4261 0 R
/Next 4265 0 R
>>
endobj
4264 0 obj
<<
/Title (Transition to On-Board Edge Computing \(Jetson Nano Integration\) Currently, the system relies on a remote PC for vision processing, which introduces a dependency on a local Wi- Fi network and a specific communication radius. Transitioning the vision processing to an on-board module, such as an NVIDIA Jetson Nano or Orin Nano, would eliminate the latency inherent in Wi-Fi-based MJPEG streaming. By performing "Inference at the Edge," the drone could achieve sub-10ms response times. This would allow the AeroEye system to track targets moving at high velocities while operating in remote or "denied" locations where no external computing infrastructure or local area networks are available.)
/Dest [106 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 4266 0 R
/Next 4262 0 R
>>
endobj
